import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"The Typechecker is Handl, Not Rust","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"The Typechecker is Handl, Not Rust","type":"adr","date":"2026-09-10T00:00:00.000Z","status":"accepted","status_note":"Accepted — Phases 1–2 complete, Phase 3 in progress, Phase 4 pending,\\nPhase 5 in progress (this update). The Handl typecheck models are\\nauthored and parse; the `HandlTypecheckEngine` adapter compiles and\\npasses 23 tests; the adapter is wired into `kit-canonical`. The models\\nare skeletons — full typechecking is not yet working end-to-end. The\\nRust typecheck crates are NOT deleted (pending production-ready models)."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/adrs/0105-typechecker-in-handl.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/adrs/0105-typechecker-in-handl.md"}'),a={name:`handl/project/adrs/0105-typechecker-in-handl.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0105-the-typechecker-is-handl-not-rust" tabindex="-1">ADR-0105: The Typechecker is Handl, Not Rust <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0105-the-typechecker-is-handl-not-rust" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0105: The Typechecker is Handl, Not Rust”">​</a></h1><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>ADR-0103 established that the kernel is generic evaluator/VM infrastructure, not the calculus. Five Handl-authored models were created: <code>exec_model.hnl</code>, <code>arrow_model.hnl</code>, <code>type_model.hnl</code>, <code>meta_model.hnl</code>, and <code>value_model.hnl</code>. The <code>Term</code> → <code>TermData</code> migration is in progress (4,311 → ~3,086 references migrated so far; 1,225 migrated across bytecode compiler, tree-walk engine, Cranelift compiler, refinement engine (partial), <code>handl-language</code> (partial), NBE typechecker (<code>lib.rs</code>), <code>handl-runtime</code> (tests), <code>plugin-engine</code>).</p><p>Three Rust crates currently own typechecking:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Crate</th><th>Lines</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>plugin-engine-typecheck</code></td><td>~1,500</td><td><code>TypecheckEngine</code> trait + <code>bootstrap.rs</code> (scope/import checker)</td></tr><tr><td><code>plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe</code></td><td>~5,500 + 11,364 tests</td><td>NBE engine: AST walk, context, unification, dependent types</td></tr><tr><td><code>plugin-lib-lang-typecheck</code></td><td>~229</td><td>Host function <code>typecheck.typecheck(lang, ast)</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p><code>type_model.hnl</code> (817 lines, extended from 459) covers HoTT tag-to-judgment interpretation — now with 26 new judgment ops (unification, metavariables, transport, and <code>Src</code>/<code>Tgt</code>/<code>CellId</code>/ <code>CellCompV</code>/<code>Whisker</code>/<code>Univalence</code>/<code>Glue</code>/<code>Fibrant</code>/<code>JElim</code>/ <code>RecordProj</code>/<code>RecordWith</code> tag arms) — but not the surrounding driver: AST traversal, typing context Γ, unification, metavariables, dependent-type closures, predicate evaluation, totality checking, or module-level scope checks. Those are the job of the three new models authored in Phase 1 (below).</p><p>The bootstrap problem: <code>kit-canonical</code> hard-wires <code>NbeTypecheckEngine::new(...)</code> at compile time. But the tree-walk eval engine is already available when the kit is built, so a Handl typecheck model can be loaded as a <code>.hnl</code> module and interpreted by the tree-walk engine — no precompilation or two-stage bootstrap needed.</p><p>Key finding: <code>hnl typecheck</code> currently uses <code>bootstrap.rs</code> (<code>check_module_with_prelude</code>), NOT the NBE <code>TypecheckEngine</code>. <code>hnl run</code>/ <code>eval</code>/<code>test</code> skip typechecking entirely. The NBE engine is wired into <code>Runtime::typecheck</code> / <code>Runtime::run_checked</code> / <code>Kit::run</code> but not exercised by the CLI&#39;s normal paths. This means the migration can proceed without breaking the dogfood gate.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><p>Delete all three typecheck Rust crates. Replace with Handl-authored typechecking models. Keep only a thin Rust <code>TypecheckEngine</code> trait and a <code>HandlTypecheckEngine</code> adapter that delegates to the Handl models.</p><h3 id="architecture" tabindex="-1">Architecture <a class="header-anchor" href="#architecture" aria-label="Permalink to “Architecture”">​</a></h3><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>Kernel (Rust, irreducible):</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  - TypecheckEngine trait (the contract)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  - HandlTypecheckEngine adapter (marshals Language + Ast, calls model)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  - Runtime registration (resolve engine by name)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span></span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Typechecking (Handl, compiled to bytecode):</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  - typecheck_model.hnl   — the driver: AST walk, Γ, unification, dispatch</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  - type_model.hnl        — HoTT tag-to-judgment interpretation (exists)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  - scope_model.hnl       — module-level scope/import/export checks</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  - totality_model.hnl    — termination/totality checking</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id="what-stays-in-rust" tabindex="-1">What stays in Rust <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-in-rust" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays in Rust”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>TypecheckEngine</code> trait (~30 lines) — the Rust contract that <code>handl-runtime</code> dispatches over. Moves to <code>plugin-engine</code> or <code>handl-runtime</code> itself.</li><li><code>TypecheckRequest</code> / <code>TypecheckResult</code> / <code>TypecheckDiagnostic</code> — the data types crossing the Rust ↔ Handl boundary.</li><li><code>HandlTypecheckEngine</code> — a thin adapter that: <ol><li>Loads the typecheck model(s) from embedded <code>.hnl</code> source.</li><li>Marshals <code>Language</code> (as <code>Value</code>) and <code>Ast</code> (as <code>Value</code>) into the model&#39;s expected format.</li><li>Calls the model&#39;s <code>typecheck(lang, ast)</code> function via the tree-walk eval engine.</li><li>Unmarshals <code>TypecheckResult</code> from the returned <code>Value</code>.</li></ol></li><li><code>TypecheckFn</code> in <code>plugin-lib-lang-typecheck</code> — the host function behind <code>typecheck.typecheck(lang, ast)</code>. Unchanged: it already calls <code>handle.typecheck(&amp;ast)</code>.</li></ul><h3 id="what-moves-to-handl" tabindex="-1">What moves to Handl <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-moves-to-handl" aria-label="Permalink to “What moves to Handl”">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>NBE component</th><th>Handl replacement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>eval_type_scheme</code> (tag dispatch)</td><td><code>type_model.hnl</code> <code>run</code> (exists)</td></tr><tr><td><code>eval_judgment</code> (~50 ops)</td><td><code>typecheck_model.hnl</code> judgment ops</td></tr><tr><td><code>synth_node</code> / <code>check_node</code> (AST walk)</td><td><code>typecheck_model.hnl</code> synth/check</td></tr><tr><td>Γ management (extend, lookup, bind)</td><td><code>typecheck_model.hnl</code> context ops</td></tr><tr><td>Unification + metavariables</td><td><code>typecheck_model.hnl</code> unify</td></tr><tr><td>Dependent-type closures (Pi/Sigma/Forall/Vau)</td><td><code>typecheck_model.hnl</code></td></tr><tr><td>Predicate evaluation</td><td><code>typecheck_model.hnl</code> (or <code>predicate_model.hnl</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>Totality checking</td><td><code>totality_model.hnl</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>bootstrap.rs</code> scope/import/export checks</td><td><code>scope_model.hnl</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="bootstrap-solution" tabindex="-1">Bootstrap solution <a class="header-anchor" href="#bootstrap-solution" aria-label="Permalink to “Bootstrap solution”">​</a></h3><p>No two-stage bootstrap needed. The tree-walk eval engine (<code>TreeWalkEngine</code>) is instantiated in <code>kit-canonical</code> before the typecheck engine is registered. The <code>HandlTypecheckEngine</code> adapter:</p><ol><li>Embeds the <code>.hnl</code> model source at compile time (<code>include_str!</code>).</li><li>At registration time, parses + loads the model into a <code>HandlModule</code>.</li><li>When <code>typecheck()</code> is called, invokes the model&#39;s <code>typecheck</code> function via the tree-walk engine.</li></ol><p>This works because the tree-walk engine does not depend on the typechecker — it depends only on <code>plugin-engine-exec</code> (the eval abstraction) and <code>handl-language</code> (the <code>Language</code>/<code>Ast</code> types).</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><h3 id="positive" tabindex="-1">Positive <a class="header-anchor" href="#positive" aria-label="Permalink to “Positive”">​</a></h3><ul><li>Typechecking logic becomes data, not Rust. Adding a type rule is a data change (YAML + Handl model), not an engine recompile.</li><li>The HoTT/type theory is fully auditable as Handl code.</li><li>The 5,500-line NBE engine + 1,081-line bootstrap + 1,076-line predicate evaluator + 407-line totality checker = ~8,064 lines of Rust deleted.</li><li>The <code>Term</code> enum loses its largest consumer (1,248 references).</li><li>ADR-0103 reaches its end state for the typechecker.</li></ul><h3 id="negative" tabindex="-1">Negative <a class="header-anchor" href="#negative" aria-label="Permalink to “Negative”">​</a></h3><ul><li>Performance: the typechecker runs on the tree-walk VM instead of native Rust. This may be slower for large modules. Mitigation: the bytecode/cranelift engines can compile the typecheck model once the VM is mature.</li><li>The 11,364 lines of NBE tests need to be ported to test the Handl models. Many can be expressed as Handl-level parity tests; some may need new test infrastructure.</li><li>Risk of semantic drift during migration. Mitigation: keep the Rust NBE engine until parity tests pass, then delete.</li></ul><h3 id="neutral" tabindex="-1">Neutral <a class="header-anchor" href="#neutral" aria-label="Permalink to “Neutral”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>plugin-lib-lang-typecheck</code> stays (it&#39;s a thin host function).</li><li>The <code>TypecheckEngine</code> trait stays (it&#39;s the Rust contract).</li><li><code>canonical.yaml</code>&#39;s <code>runtime.typecheck: nbe</code> stays (the name is resolved to whatever engine is registered).</li></ul><h2 id="migration-plan" tabindex="-1">Migration Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#migration-plan" aria-label="Permalink to “Migration Plan”">​</a></h2><h3 id="phase-1-author-the-handl-typecheck-models-—-complete" tabindex="-1">Phase 1: Author the Handl typecheck models — COMPLETE <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-1-author-the-handl-typecheck-models-—-complete" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 1: Author the Handl typecheck models — COMPLETE”">​</a></h3><p>All four models authored and parse successfully:</p><ol><li><p><strong><code>typecheck_model.hnl</code></strong> (1,305 lines) — the driver:</p><ul><li><code>typecheck(lang, ast)</code> entry point</li><li>AST walk via <code>lang.types[node.kind]</code> → <code>TypeRuleDef</code> → <code>synth</code>/<code>check</code></li><li>Γ context management (extend, lookup, bind, result)</li><li>Judgment ops (~50): <code>eval_child</code>, <code>proj_child</code>, <code>unify</code>, <code>bind</code>, <code>result</code>, <code>eval_scheme</code>, <code>fresh_meta</code>, <code>solve_meta</code>, etc.</li><li>Dependent-type closures: Pi, Sigma, Forall, Vau</li><li>Unification + metavariable store</li><li>Delegates tag interpretation to <code>type_model.hnl</code></li></ul></li><li><p><strong><code>scope_model.hnl</code></strong> (801 lines) — module-level checks (replaces <code>bootstrap.rs</code>):</p><ul><li>Collect bindings (imports, exports, <code>name = expr</code>)</li><li>Detect duplicates</li><li>Unbound-wire detection</li><li>Unused-import detection</li><li><code>rec</code> region well-formedness</li></ul></li><li><p><strong><code>totality_model.hnl</code></strong> (718 lines) — termination checking:</p><ul><li><code>check_totality(ast, expr_ref, lang)</code></li><li>Decreasing argument/field detection</li><li>Measure-based termination</li></ul></li><li><p><strong><code>type_model.hnl</code></strong> extended from 459 to 817 lines with 26 new HoTT judgment ops (unification, metavariables, transport, and <code>Src</code>/<code>Tgt</code>/<code>CellId</code>/<code>CellCompV</code>/<code>Whisker</code>/<code>Univalence</code>/<code>Glue</code>/ <code>Fibrant</code>/<code>JElim</code>/<code>RecordProj</code>/<code>RecordWith</code> tag arms).</p></li></ol><p><strong>Caveat:</strong> the models parse and load, but they are skeletons — the judgment ops and AST-walk logic are structurally complete but not yet semantically validated against the Rust NBE engine. Full typechecking is not yet working end-to-end.</p><h3 id="phase-2-write-the-handltypecheckengine-adapter-—-complete" tabindex="-1">Phase 2: Write the <code>HandlTypecheckEngine</code> adapter — COMPLETE <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-2-write-the-handltypecheckengine-adapter-—-complete" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 2: Write the HandlTypecheckEngine adapter — COMPLETE”">​</a></h3><ol><li><p><code>HandlTypecheckEngine</code> created in a new thin crate <code>plugin-engine-typecheck-handl</code>:</p><ul><li><code>new(eval_engine: Box&lt;dyn EvalEngine&gt;) -&gt; Self</code></li><li>Embeds model source via <code>include_str!</code></li><li>Loads models into <code>HandlModule</code> at construction, wiring stdlib <code>array</code>/<code>hash_map</code>/<code>typeof</code>/<code>tag</code> dependencies</li><li><code>typecheck(&amp;self, lang, req)</code> marshals <code>Language</code> + <code>Ast</code> to <code>Value</code>, calls model, unmarshals <code>TypecheckResult</code></li><li>Implements <code>TypecheckEngine</code> trait</li><li>Graceful degradation: if the model fails to load, returns <code>LangError::NotImplemented</code> (the crate always compiles)</li></ul></li><li><p><code>TypecheckEngine</code> trait + <code>TypecheckRequest</code>/<code>Result</code>/<code>Diagnostic</code> remain in <code>plugin-engine-typecheck</code> (not yet moved).</p></li></ol><p><strong>Test status:</strong> 23 tests pass (6 unit in <code>lib.rs</code> + 14 in <code>handl_typecheck_parity.rs</code> + 3 in <code>integration.rs</code>).</p><h3 id="phase-3-wire-and-verify-—-in-progress" tabindex="-1">Phase 3: Wire and verify — IN PROGRESS <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-3-wire-and-verify-—-in-progress" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 3: Wire and verify — IN PROGRESS”">​</a></h3><ol><li>✅ <code>HandlTypecheckEngine</code> registered in <code>kit-canonical</code> under the <code>&quot;nbe&quot;</code> name (alongside the existing <code>NbeTypecheckEngine</code>).</li><li>⏳ <code>hnl typecheck</code> still routes through <code>check_module_with_prelude</code> (not yet switched to <code>Kit::typecheck</code>).</li><li>⏳ NBE tests not yet ported as Handl-level parity tests.</li><li>⏳ Dogfood gate testing in progress — the adapter is wired but the models return errors when called (graceful degradation); the gate still passes because <code>hnl typecheck</code> uses the bootstrap path.</li><li>⏳ 177 corpus files not yet verified through the Handl models.</li></ol><p><strong>Stdlib wiring fix:</strong> the adapter now wires <code>array</code>, <code>hash_map</code>, <code>typeof</code>, and <code>tag</code> modules as dependencies of the typecheck model (via <code>with_dependency</code> in <code>HandlTypecheckEngine::new</code>). Without this, the model failed to load because it calls <code>array.first</code>, <code>hash_map.get</code>, <code>typeof.type_of</code>, and <code>tag.tag</code> at runtime.</p><h3 id="phase-4-delete-the-rust-crates-—-pending" tabindex="-1">Phase 4: Delete the Rust crates — PENDING <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-4-delete-the-rust-crates-—-pending" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 4: Delete the Rust crates — PENDING”">​</a></h3><p>Cannot proceed until the Handl models are production-ready (full typechecking working end-to-end with parity against the NBE engine).</p><ol><li>Delete <code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck-nbe/</code> (the NBE engine).</li><li>Delete <code>crates/plugin-engine-typecheck/</code> (the bootstrap checker). <ul><li>Move <code>TypecheckEngine</code> trait to <code>plugin-engine</code> or <code>handl-runtime</code> first.</li></ul></li><li>Update <code>kit-canonical</code> to use <code>HandlTypecheckEngine</code>.</li><li>Update <code>host-cli</code> to use <code>Kit::typecheck</code> instead of <code>check_module_with_prelude</code>.</li><li>Update <code>Cargo.toml</code> workspace members.</li><li>Update all downstream <code>Cargo.toml</code> dependencies.</li></ol><h3 id="phase-5-update-adrs-—-in-progress-this-update" tabindex="-1">Phase 5: Update ADRs — IN PROGRESS (this update) <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-5-update-adrs-—-in-progress-this-update" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 5: Update ADRs — IN PROGRESS (this update)”">​</a></h3><p>ADR-0103 updated with the new models, adapter, Term:: reference counts, and ADR-0105 cross-reference. ADR-0105 status changed from Proposed to Accepted. ADR-0103&#39;s typechecker migration will be marked complete once Phase 4 (delete Rust crates) is done.</p><h2 id="current-state" tabindex="-1">Current state <a class="header-anchor" href="#current-state" aria-label="Permalink to “Current state”">​</a></h2><h3 id="what-works" tabindex="-1">What works <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-works" aria-label="Permalink to “What works”">​</a></h3><ul><li>All four models (<code>typecheck_model.hnl</code>, <code>scope_model.hnl</code>, <code>totality_model.hnl</code>, extended <code>type_model.hnl</code>) parse and load via the <code>HandlModule</code> loader.</li><li><code>HandlTypecheckEngine</code> adapter compiles and implements the <code>TypecheckEngine</code> trait.</li><li>23 tests pass: model loading, type-model tag interpretation, typecheck-driver smoke tests, totality-model smoke tests, and integration tests (adapter construction + typecheck invocation).</li><li>The adapter is wired into <code>kit-canonical</code> (registered under <code>&quot;nbe&quot;</code>).</li><li>Stdlib dependencies (<code>array</code>, <code>hash_map</code>, <code>typeof</code>, <code>tag</code>) are wired into the adapter so the model loads successfully.</li></ul><h3 id="what-doesn-t-work-yet" tabindex="-1">What doesn&#39;t work yet <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-doesn-t-work-yet" aria-label="Permalink to “What doesn&#39;t work yet”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Models are skeletons.</strong> The judgment ops and AST-walk logic are structurally authored but not semantically validated. Calling <code>typecheck(lang, ast)</code> on a real program returns errors (graceful degradation — the adapter returns <code>LangError::NotImplemented</code> or the model returns diagnostics).</li><li><strong>Full typechecking is not working end-to-end.</strong> No real program has been successfully typechecked through the Handl models.</li><li><strong><code>hnl typecheck</code> still uses the Rust bootstrap path</strong> (<code>check_module_with_prelude</code>), not the Handl models. The dogfood gate is unaffected.</li><li><strong>stdlib <code>array.is_empty.hnl</code> has a parse error.</strong> This does not block the adapter (the model loads without it), but it is a known gap to fix.</li><li><strong>NBE test suite not ported.</strong> The 11,364 lines of NBE tests have not been ported to Handl-level parity tests.</li><li><strong>Rust typecheck crates are NOT deleted.</strong> They remain in the workspace and are still the production typechecker.</li></ul><h3 id="commit-history-this-session" tabindex="-1">Commit history (this session) <a class="header-anchor" href="#commit-history-this-session" aria-label="Permalink to “Commit history (this session)”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>152932ad</code> — feat: author Handl typecheck models and adapter for ADR-0105 (Phase 1 + Phase 2: models + adapter crate).</li><li><code>a2b5b11f</code> — feat: wire HandlTypecheckEngine into kit-canonical with parity tests (Phase 3 start: wiring + 23 tests).</li><li><code>d017b4b7</code> — feat: wire stdlib deps in adapter and extend type_model.hnl with HoTT ops (stdlib fix + 26 new judgment ops).</li></ul><h2 id="open-questions" tabindex="-1">Open Questions <a class="header-anchor" href="#open-questions" aria-label="Permalink to “Open Questions”">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Performance</strong>: Is the tree-walk engine fast enough for typechecking 177-file corpus? If not, can the bytecode engine compile the typecheck model?</li><li><strong>Test porting</strong>: The 11,364 lines of NBE tests cover many edge cases. How many can be directly ported to Handl-level tests vs. needing new test infrastructure?</li><li><strong><code>plugin-lib-lang-typecheck</code></strong>: Does this crate stay as-is, or does it also get absorbed into the Handl model? (Currently it&#39;s a thin host function — likely stays.)</li><li><strong>Type registry</strong>: <code>NbeTypecheckEngine</code> uses <code>handl-plugin-lib-tag::TypeRegistry</code> to mint type values. Does this stay as a Rust host primitive, or does the type model construct type values directly?</li></ol>`,52)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};